    "done_when": "Context: followup f-fsri-ladder-census-counts-every-entry in forward-solver-route-integrity. benchmarks/recovery_ladder_census.py counts two of the five promotion and recovery entries defined in nova/equilibrium/fixed_point.py, so its reported 19.03 percent instruction share is a lower bound. Its instrumented() skips a counted path absent from the module, so a renamed rung reads as zero executions rather than failing, and the report names a revision one commit behind the tree that carries it. Repair: count every promotion and recovery entry fixed_point.py defines, enumerated from the module rather than hand-listed where possible; raise naming any counted path that is absent; and stamp the committing revision in the report. Add tests/test_recovery_ladder_census.py, which fails when a counted rung is renamed. Gate, logged under the run directory: the new test passes with JAX_PLATFORMS=cpu in place on this fleet allocation, and fails under the negative control run from a full tree copy with --import-mode=importlib and the module __file__ printed. The repaired census re-runs on one certificate row and reports the five entries with per-solve execution counts and instruction shares. Benchmarks and tests only, no edit to nova/. Every uv command carries --no-sync and nothing runs uv sync. The manifest's status is one of complete, blocked or failed.",
